 - Accessibility and readability controls: preview text and controls over the image, configurable approved overlay/contrast treatment, and reduced-motion behavior. **The fallback background used whenever a remotely managed background fails to load must be the exact approved launch background shipped with the initial release of the Mawadda platform/app.** Keep this launch background bundled locally in the app/web assets so it remains available offline and during network or CDN failures. It is the stable default fallback across supported devices until the owner explicitly publishes a replacement fallback through the same reviewed and versioned background-management workflow. A failed or invalid remote asset must never leave a blank surface or silently substitute an unrelated image.
 - Draft/preview/publish/rollback workflow consistent with section 17.3. Publication is atomic; each change records owner UID, timestamp, placement, asset/version identifiers, reason and prior/new configuration in the immutable audit trail.
